From 7c46108743ca8fe2e977210ecd1be73821fc2d3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:18:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 93/99] dock: Runs a launcher's PasteCommand on the middle
 button.

As Window Maker's PasteCommand: The middle button on a launcher of the
Dock, the Clip or a drawer reads the selection (the primary selection,
else the clipboard) and runs the command with "%s" replaced by it.

The command runs through `/bin/sh -c`, as on Window Maker; "%s" becomes
"$@", with the selection given as argument: It is not parsed by the
shell. The selection is read from the event loop, within 5 seconds.
Without a PasteCommand, the button goes to `wlmdock` as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
